commit 61a5a18f64c73cd4e4dffa71b9ed872582e826c5
Author: Bobby <zkd8907@live.com>
Date:   Sun Aug 23 13:30:40 2026 +0800

    Let preflight admit the providers this repo already ships
    
    generate-tencent-image.mjs, generate-voice.mjs and providers.md all support
    the Tencent paths, but preflight's three whitelists never learned about them,
    so the only credentialed combination on a machine with Tencent keys was the
    one it refused. Adds tencent-aiart, tencent, and a synthesis timing provider
    that reads per-sentence durations from the synthesizer instead of recovering
    them with ASR -- generate-voice.mjs already writes that sidecar and
    apply-caption-timings.mjs already reads it. Credentials are checked here too,
    so a missing key fails before the thirtieth image rather than during it.
    
    A real artifact -- a screenshot, terminal capture, or diagram the story is
    actually about -- may now enter a scene as its own alpha layer, unaltered.
    Its value is that it is the thing rather than a drawing of it. It rides inside
    the frame; it still cannot become the frame, and the layer contract's hard
    failures are untouched.
    
    The watermark section was wrong. Tencent's API reference says LogoAdd defaults
    to 1 and 0 omits the mark, stated identically on three interfaces. The old
    claim that the mark survived LogoAdd: 0 is withdrawn, with the likely cause
    noted -- a call that never passed the flag -- and the question left open until
    a generated image has been looked at.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

